@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
title Python environments — detected and provisioned, never inherited

' covers: packages/lib/entrypoint-lib.sh, defs/opencode/entrypoint.sh,
'         defs/cursor/entrypoint.sh, defs/cecli/entrypoint.sh,
'         defs/claudecode/mcp/entrypoint.sh

node "Host" as HOST <<host>> {
  database "miniconda / venv\nabsolute paths · macOS binaries" as HOSTENV <<error>>
  database "workspace ""\.venv""\nbin/python → host interpreter" as HOSTVENV <<error>>
}

node "Container — ensure_python_env" as C <<host>> {
  component "**detect** — ""_py_project_kind""\nconda · uv · poetry · pip" as KIND <<app>>
  component "**capability** — ""_py_venv_capable""\nnot ""command -v python3""" as CAP <<app>>
  component "**provision** — mise\npython@X · uv · poetry · micromamba" as PROV <<app>>
  component "**build** — ""_py_build_env""\nper-kind installer" as BUILD <<app>>
  component "**activate** — VIRTUAL_ENV + PATH" as ACT <<app>>
}

database "PROVEO_HOME\n""~/.cache/proveo/venv/<hash>""" as ENV <<db>>
component "pyright\nresolves real packages" as PYRIGHT <<app>>

KIND ARROW_MAIN CAP
CAP ARROW_MAIN PROV : only when the image cannot
PROV ARROW_MAIN BUILD
BUILD ARROW_MAIN ENV : outside the workspace
ENV ARROW_MAIN ACT
ACT ARROW_MAIN PYRIGHT : VIRTUAL_ENV
HOSTENV ARROW_ERROR C : cannot cross the boundary
HOSTVENV ARROW_ERROR ACT : shadowed, with a warning

note bottom of HOSTENV
  **A host environment cannot be inherited, on three counts.** ""pyvenv\.cfg"" and
  ""activate"" hardcode absolute host paths; ""bin/python"" is a SYMLINK to the host
  interpreter, which dangles in the container; and — fatally — the interpreter
  and every compiled extension in ""site-packages"" are host-OS/arch binaries.
  A macOS arm64 ""\.so"" cannot execute on Linux at any path, so even mounting the
  whole conda prefix at an identical path fails.

  This is the ""node_modules"" native-binary hazard, but stricter: node_modules is
  often pure JavaScript, whereas a venv ALWAYS contains a platform interpreter.
end note

note right of CAP
  **Presence is not capability.** ""python3-minimal"" arrives as a transitive apt
  dependency, so ""command -v python3"" succeeds on most harnesses while
  ""python3 -m venv"" fails — Debian splits ensurepip out. Probing the capability
  rather than the binary is what stops a decoy interpreter being mistaken for a
  usable one, the same lesson as clangd installing but not executing.

  No harness ships a usable general-purpose Python: two have the decoy, cecli's
  belongs to its own agent venv, and cursor has none. So there is nothing to
  share and no ""base-python"" layer to build — Python is detected and
  provisioned, exactly like Go.
end note

note right of PROV
  **mise is the mechanism, not a competitor to uv.** It is already on the floor
  provisioning eight language servers, and its registry carries ""uv"",
  ""poetry"" and ""micromamba"" — so the Python tool a project needs is just
  another recipe, with the bounded timeouts, GitHub auth and idempotence
  ""_mise_install"" already provides.

  Measured: interpreter 17s cold and 0s warm, identical to uv's own warm path.
  Choosing a second mechanism would buy speed that PROVEO_HOME already gives.
end note

note bottom of ENV
  Built OUTSIDE the workspace and keyed by workspace path, so it can never
  collide with the developer's own ""\.venv"" and never lands in a mounted tree
  that may be read-only. Persisting under PROVEO_HOME is what makes the second
  run 1s instead of 18s.
end note

note bottom of PYRIGHT
  The payoff. pyright is already baked into the LSP images but, with no
  environment to introspect, resolves no third-party package — it reports
  ""reportMissingModuleSource"" and falls back to bundled stubs. It honours
  ""VIRTUAL_ENV"", so activation alone fixes it; no extra LSP config is needed.
end note
@enduml
